  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let G be a discrete countable group, given as a central extension 0 → Z →\nG → Q → 0. Assume that either G is quasi-isometric to Z × Q, or that Z → G is a\nquasi-isometric embedding. Does that imply that G comes from a bounded cocycle\non Q?                                                         I. Chatterji, G. Mislin",
